;; refuse-runtime: defprotocol is not supported on the WasmGC target
;; refuse-llvm: satisfies? of a protocol not named at the call (protocols are not values on the llvm target)
;; A protocol taken from a collection is a value. Natively satisfies? takes
;; any protocol value; the llvm lane answers satisfies? only for a protocol
;; named at the call (corpus/poly/protocols.lg), and the GC lane raises its
;; named limit for protocols when the program runs.
(defprotocol Named (nm [this]))
(def protocols [Named])
(println (satisfies? (first protocols) "s"))
